---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { u } from '../i18n';
---

<Base
  lang="en"
  page="whatsapp"
  title={'Inside WhatsApp Desktop’s session setup · CryptoBAP'}
  description={
    'How does a closed-source desktop application initialise an end-to-end encrypted session, and what does that process reveal to an observer? These recordings trace the cryptographic logic of WhatsApp Desktop on macOS with the LLDB debugger, verifying communication states and the triggers that start a session.'
  }
>
  <section class="phero grain">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Case study</p>
      <h1 class="phero__title">Inside WhatsApp Desktop’s session setup</h1>
      <p class="lead phero__lead">
        How does a closed-source desktop application initialise an end-to-end encrypted session, and
        what does that process reveal to an observer? These recordings trace the cryptographic logic
        of WhatsApp Desktop on macOS with the LLDB debugger, verifying communication states and the
        triggers that start a session.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <!-- ── Headline finding ─────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section--tight">
    <div class="container">
      <aside class="wa-finding" data-reveal>
        <div class="wa-finding__mark" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="1.6"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
          >
            <path d="M12 3 3.5 7.2v5.1c0 4.6 3.5 8.3 8.5 9.4 5-1.1 8.5-4.8 8.5-9.4V7.2Z"></path>
            <path d="M12 8.6v4.2M12 16.2h.01"></path>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="wa-finding__label">Headline finding</p>
          <p class="wa-finding__body">
            Under the constant-time observation model, instruction-cache behaviour during session
            establishment distinguishes whether a conversation with a given recipient already exists
            — enough to infer parts of a user’s social graph.
          </p>
          <p class="wa-finding__cite">
            Automated Side-Channel Analysis of Cryptographic Protocol Implementations, CCS 2026
          </p>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>
  <!-- ── Videos ───────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="vsplit">
        <div class="vsplit__copy" data-reveal>
          <p class="eyebrow">Recording 01</p>
          <h2 class="vsplit__title">Technical flow analysis &amp; debugging logic</h2>
          <p class="prose vsplit__purpose">
            A step-by-step methodology for using LLDB to observe the execution flow of cryptographic
            functions, focused on the triggers that fire during UI interactions — starting a new
            chat with a contact, or creating a group.
          </p>
          <ul class="list-check vsplit__points">
            <li>
              <span>
                Attach to the WhatsApp process and set a breakpoint on{' '}
                <code>session_builder_process_pre_key_bundle</code>.
              </span>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span>
                Identify the memory addresses that signal no existing conversation with a recipient.
              </span>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span>
                Take a backtrace to map the call stack of the Signal Protocol implementation.
              </span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="vsplit__video" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay:90ms">
          <figure class="vid">
            <div
              class="vid__frame"
              data-video
              data-src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/CDuQIf1oPjA?si=s6AZRQXFs9ph4tAa&amp;autoplay=1&amp;rel=0"
              data-title="Debugging WhatsApp Session Initialization with LLDB on macOS"
            >
              <button
                class="vid__btn"
                type="button"
                aria-label="Play video: Debugging WhatsApp Session Initialization with LLDB on macOS"
              >
                <picture>
                  <source srcset={u('media/thumb-CDuQIf1oPjA.webp')} type="image/webp" />
                  <img
                    src={u('media/thumb-CDuQIf1oPjA.jpg')}
                    alt=""
                    width="1280"
                    height="720"
                    loading="lazy"
                    decoding="async"
                  />
                </picture>
                <span class="vid__scrim" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                <span class="vid__play" aria-hidden="true">
                  <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor">
                    <path d="M8 5.5v13a1 1 0 0 0 1.53.85l10.2-6.5a1 1 0 0 0 0-1.7L9.53 4.65A1 1 0 0 0 8 5.5Z"></path>
                  </svg>
                </span>
                <span class="vid__meta" aria-hidden="true">
                  <span class="vid__label">01</span>
                  <span class="vid__title">
                    Debugging WhatsApp Session Initialization with LLDB on macOS
                  </span>
                </span>
              </button>
            </div>
            <figcaption class="vid__cap">
              <span class="vid__privacy">
                <svg
                  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                  width="13"
                  height="13"
                  fill="none"
                  stroke="currentColor"
                  stroke-width="1.7"
                  aria-hidden="true"
                >
                  <rect x="4" y="10.5" width="16" height="10" rx="2.2"></rect>
                  <path d="M8 10.5V7.4a4 4 0 1 1 8 0v3.1"></path>
                </svg>
                <span>Playing the video connects to YouTube.</span>
              </span>
              <a
                class="vid__direct"
                href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CDuQIf1oPjA"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >
                Watch on YouTube <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
              </a>
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
          <script type="module">
            document.querySelectorAll(`[data-video]`).forEach((e) => {
              e.querySelector(`button`)?.addEventListener(`click`, () => {
                let t = document.createElement(`iframe`);
                ((t.src = e.dataset.src ?? ``),
                  (t.title = e.dataset.title ?? ``),
                  (t.allow = `accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share`),
                  (t.referrerPolicy = `strict-origin-when-cross-origin`),
                  (t.allowFullscreen = !0),
                  e.replaceChildren(t),
                  t.focus());
              });
            });
          </script>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section band">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="vsplit">
        <div class="vsplit__copy" data-reveal>
          <p class="eyebrow">Recording 02</p>
          <h2 class="vsplit__title">End-to-end lifecycle &amp; security analysis</h2>
          <p class="prose vsplit__purpose">
            Moving beyond logical tracing to a security-centric audit of the E2E session lifecycle:
            the boundaries around account-level events, and how communication states are managed
            across device transitions.
          </p>
          <ul class="list-check vsplit__points">
            <li>
              <span>
                The full lifecycle, from registration and account setup through to conversation
                deletion.
              </span>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span>
                The security implications of attacker re-registration and linking the desktop client
                to a new account.
              </span>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span>
                How the application retrieves key bundles and maintains secure state across multiple
                contacts.
              </span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="vsplit__video" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay:90ms">
          <figure class="vid">
            <div
              class="vid__frame"
              data-video
              data-src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/feWSc6SY4Mw?si=dKvamS4T07uRHIxL&amp;autoplay=1&amp;rel=0"
              data-title="WhatsApp Security Analysis: Reverse Engineering E2E Session Setup"
            >
              <button
                class="vid__btn"
                type="button"
                aria-label="Play video: WhatsApp Security Analysis: Reverse Engineering E2E Session Setup"
              >
                <picture>
                  <source srcset={u('media/thumb-feWSc6SY4Mw.webp')} type="image/webp" />
                  <img
                    src={u('media/thumb-feWSc6SY4Mw.jpg')}
                    alt=""
                    width="1280"
                    height="720"
                    loading="lazy"
                    decoding="async"
                  />
                </picture>
                <span class="vid__scrim" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                <span class="vid__play" aria-hidden="true">
                  <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor">
                    <path d="M8 5.5v13a1 1 0 0 0 1.53.85l10.2-6.5a1 1 0 0 0 0-1.7L9.53 4.65A1 1 0 0 0 8 5.5Z"></path>
                  </svg>
                </span>
                <span class="vid__meta" aria-hidden="true">
                  <span class="vid__label">02</span>
                  <span class="vid__title">
                    WhatsApp Security Analysis: Reverse Engineering E2E Session Setup
                  </span>
                </span>
              </button>
            </div>
            <figcaption class="vid__cap">
              <span class="vid__privacy">
                <svg
                  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                  width="13"
                  height="13"
                  fill="none"
                  stroke="currentColor"
                  stroke-width="1.7"
                  aria-hidden="true"
                >
                  <rect x="4" y="10.5" width="16" height="10" rx="2.2"></rect>
                  <path d="M8 10.5V7.4a4 4 0 1 1 8 0v3.1"></path>
                </svg>
                <span>Playing the video connects to YouTube.</span>
              </span>
              <a
                class="vid__direct"
                href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=feWSc6SY4Mw"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >
                Watch on YouTube <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
              </a>
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <!-- ── Method ───────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section--tight method-wrap">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="method" data-reveal>
        <div>
          <h2 class="method__title">Method</h2>
          <p class="method__body">
            Dynamic analysis with LLDB establishes where the interesting cryptographic work happens
            in the binary. That region is then handed to the CryptoBAP pipeline, which lifts it,
            instruments it with a leakage contract and extracts a model for the verifiers.
          </p>
        </div>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href={u('technical/')}>
          How the pipeline works
          <svg
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            width="15"
            height="15"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="1.8"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
            aria-hidden="true"
          >
            <path d="M5 12h13M13 6l6 6-6 6"></path>
          </svg>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
